# Trivy ignore file — accepted HIGH advisories (0 CRITICAL) in the runtime images.
# Reviewed 2026-06-21 (see docs/production-readiness/risk-register.md PR-014). The Trivy gate is
# BLOCKING (deploy-checks.yml exit-code 1); every entry is an explicit, justified acceptance and the
# gate still FAILS on any NEW package/advisory not listed here (allowlist model, like .secrets.baseline).
#
# OS/debian base layers scan 0 HIGH/CRITICAL. Root-cause fixes landed (2026-06-21):
#   - next: upgraded 14 -> 15.5.x — FIXED (the 5 next advisories CVE-2026-44573/44578 + GHSA-8h8q/h25m/
#     q4gf are gone), so they are intentionally NOT listed (the gate fails if they reappear).
#   - glob / tmp (dev-only build tooling via jest / @nestjs/cli): the runtime images now do a CLEAN
#     prod-only install (`rm -rf node_modules && npm ci --omit=dev` in apps/{api,web}/Dockerfile), so
#     these are ABSENT from the image — verified gone, NOT listed.
#
# Two transitive advisories genuinely persist in the prod image and are accepted:
#
# ── picomatch 4.0.1 (transitive) — Regular-expression Denial of Service (ReDoS) ──────────────────────
# HIGH, 0 CRITICAL. picomatch is a PROD transitive (pulled by next 15's dependency tree, also by
# build tooling), so it survives the prod-only install; it is glob-matching used at build/route-scan
# time, NOT on the request path with user input. An npm `overrides` to 4.0.4 is NOT honored in this
# npm-workspaces environment (it leaves picomatch "invalid", breaking strict `npm ci` — verified).
# FOLLOW-UP: pin picomatch -> 4.0.4 once the override is honored (or when next ships a patched picomatch).
CVE-2026-33671
#
# ── multer 2.0.2 (transitive PROD dep) — Denial of Service (malformed/deeply-nested/dropped uploads) ──
# HIGH, 0 CRITICAL, no RCE. multer is HARD-PINNED to exactly 2.0.2 by @nestjs/platform-express@10.4.22
# (an exact "2.0.2", not a range); an npm override is not honored here either. A clean fix requires the
# NestJS 10 -> 11 upgrade (its platform-express depends on a patched multer). Mitigated meanwhile: the
# NestJS API is the internal facade behind edge rate-limiting (PR-011); availability-only.
# FOLLOW-UP: upgrade @nestjs/* 10 -> 11 (pulls a fixed multer), then remove these.
CVE-2026-2359
CVE-2026-3304
CVE-2026-3520
CVE-2026-5079
